# CODEOWNERS — viavitae-control
#
# The two handles below are not invented: `locals.tf` maps the `control` tier to
# ["security", "compliance"], and both are real teams in the live organization
# (measured 2026-11-03: `gh api orgs/Via-Vitae/teams --paginate` returns architects,
# compliance, dpo, legal, platform, security).
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS AND IS NOT, STATED PLAINLY
# It is a routing rule. It is not separation of duties. Each of those teams has exactly one
# member, and it is the same account (`gh api orgs/Via-Vitae/teams/<slug>/members` ->
# JourneyOfLife for all six), so an approval from a listed owner is an approval by the person
# who wrote the change. Finding VV-2026-10-003 tracks that; the remedy is a second reviewer
# (`policies/restore_peer_review.md`), not a longer CODEOWNERS file.
#
# Enforcement is also not active yet: `require_code_owner_review` in `repo_rulesets.tf` reads
# `var.branch_require_code_owner_reviews`, which defaults to `false` (`variables.tf:131-135`)
# because a one-person organization cannot approve its own pull request. Until that variable
# is `true` and `branch_required_approving_review_count >= 1`, nothing here blocks a merge.

# Default owner for everything in the control plane.
*                                @Via-Vitae/security @Via-Vitae/compliance

